NNAAMMEE
       lessecho - expand metacharacters

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       lleesssseecchhoo _[_-_o_x_] _[_-_c_x_] _[_-_p_n_] _[_-_d_n_] _[_-_m_x_] _[_-_n_n_] _[_-_e_x_] _[_-_a_] _f_i_l_e _._._.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       lleesssseecchhoo  is a program that simply echos its arguments on standard out‐
       put.  But any metacharacter in the output is preceded  by  an  "escape"
       character, which by default is a backslash.  lleesssseecchhoo is invoked inter‐
       nally by lleessss, and is not intended to be used directly by humans.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       A summary of options is included below.

       --ee_x    Specifies "_x", rather than backslash, to be the escape char  for
              metachars.   If  _x  is "-", no escape char is used and arguments
              containing metachars are surrounded by quotes instead.

       --oo_x    Specifies "_x", rather than double-quote, to be  the  open  quote
              character, which is used if the -e- option is specified.

       --cc_x    Specifies "_x" to be the close quote character.

       --pp_n    Specifies "_n" to be the open quote character, as an integer.

       --dd_n    Specifies "_n" to be the close quote character, as an integer.

       --mm_x    Specifies  "_x"  to be a metachar.  By default, no characters are
              considered metachars.

       --nn_n    Specifies "_n" to be a metachar, as an integer.

       --ff_n    Specifies "_n" to be the escape char for metachars, as  an  inte‐
              ger.

       --aa     Specifies  that  all arguments are to be quoted.  The default is
              that only arguments containing metacharacters are quoted.

